# doenerstag configuration — placeholder.
#
# This file is a placeholder. `doenerstag install` replaces it with a real
# configuration file containing the database connection, the runtime database
# password and the JWT secret, written with mode 0600.
#
#   cd /etc/doenerstag
#   DOENER_DATABASE_ROOT_PASSWORD='...' doenerstag install -o /etc/doenerstag/doenerstag.yaml
#
# It is marked as a configuration file in both packages, so an upgrade will not
# overwrite what the installer wrote here, and removing the package leaves it
# alone. Deleting it is a deliberate act, not something a package does.
#
# Every setting has a documented default, a command-line flag and an
# environment variable; see docs/09_configuration.md. The database password and
# the JWT secret may not be passed on the command line — attempting it is a
# fatal error — which is why they live in this file and nowhere else.
#
# Starting the service before the installer has run will fail: there is no
# database to connect to yet. That is why the packages neither start nor enable
# the unit.
